---
import FocusedServicePage from '../components/FocusedServicePage.astro';
const data={
 slug:'b2b-seo-services',name:'B2B SEO Services',metaTitle:'B2B SEO Services for Consultancies and Service Firms | Bright Forge',description:'B2B SEO for consultancies and service firms. Clear capability pages, buyer-focused proof and measurable enquiry paths. Discuss your current website.',
 heroTitle:'B2B SEO for Businesses That Need <span>to Make the Shortlist</span>',cta:'Discuss Your B2B Website',
 intro:['A professional-services buyer needs to understand the problem you solve, the organisations you can help and the evidence behind your offer. Traffic to a broad definition page rarely answers all of those questions.','We help consultancies and B2B service firms organise their search presence around that evaluation process. The work connects service capability, relevant sectors and published proof to a clear next step, without pretending every search click is a qualified sales opportunity.'],
 proofTitle:'Consultancy Experience,',proofHighlight:'Not a Generic B2B Claim',
 proofBody:['Our published Conscient case study concerns a UK B2B marketing consultancy serving telecoms, technology and data-centre buyers. The search challenge was making its consultancy work discoverable without reducing the website to a generic agency brochure.','The published six-month comparison reports clicks increasing from 13,200 to 15,700, while click-through rate fell from 3.3% to 2.1%. That is search-performance evidence, not proof of a particular sales pipeline or a promised return for another firm.'],
 proofLinks:[{href:'/case-studies/consulting-firm-seo/',label:'Conscient: published consultancy SEO work'},{href:'/case-studies/industrial-parts-washing-search-growth/',label:'Anonymised industrial search-performance example'}],
 sections:[
  {id:'b2b-service-ownership',eyebrow:'Service and Buyer Fit',title:'Explain What You Do',highlight:'Before Expanding the Content',body:['We identify the services you actively sell, the buying problems behind them and the pages that already support those decisions. A long list of industries is not a substitute for a credible offer in each one.'],rows:[{title:'Capability Pages',body:'Make the scope, deliverables and practical fit clear. A buyer should be able to distinguish advisory work, implementation and ongoing support without opening three interchangeable pages.'},{title:'Problem and Sector Relevance',body:'Use buyer language and examples that the actual team can support. A new sector page needs different questions and evidence, not a copied service description with another industry name.'},{title:'Proof at the Decision Point',body:'Connect appropriate case studies to service and enquiry pages. Explain the work and its limits. Do not use a search metric as a substitute for commercial outcomes that were never measured.'}],links:[{href:'/keyword-research-services/',label:'Buyer and competitor research'},{href:'/seo-audit-services/',label:'Existing-page audit'}]},
  {id:'b2b-shortlist-journey',eyebrow:'From Discovery to Evaluation',title:'Help the Buyer',highlight:'Assess the Next Step',body:['B2B purchases can involve several reviewers. One person may discover the business through a problem query while another checks the capability, evidence and contact route. We organise internal links and page content to support that evaluation rather than demand an immediate sales call from every visitor.','The plan distinguishes content that explains a problem from pages that sell a service. When an existing page can own the intent, we improve it instead of publishing a second page that competes for the same job.'],rows:[{title:'Technical Access',body:'Important service and case-study pages must be crawlable, linked and readable in the delivered page. We check the actual site output rather than rely solely on a CMS field.'},{title:'Useful Enquiry Paths',body:'A next step should fit the buying decision: discussing scope, sharing a brief or reviewing the website. We check the route and agree how a relevant enquiry will be identified where the tracking allows it.'}],links:[{href:'/technical-seo-services-philippines/',label:'Technical SEO support'},{href:'/content-seo-services-philippines/',label:'Content planning and delivery'}]},
  {id:'specialist-b2b-boundaries',eyebrow:'Different Businesses, Different Owners',title:'Use Specialist Pages',highlight:'Where the Buying Journey Changes',body:['This offer centres professional services and consultancy evaluation. Software trials, product catalogues and construction quotes introduce different requirements. They should not be hidden inside a generic B2B page or used to imply expertise in every vertical.','We use the relevant specialist scope where it fits, and confirm the experience and review resources before entering an unfamiliar sector. Published industrial search data provides a supporting example of measurement, not permission to claim undisclosed client work or results.'],links:[{href:'/saas-seo-services/',label:'SaaS, product trials and demos'},{href:'/construction-seo-services/',label:'Construction and industrial buying journeys'},{href:'/ecommerce-seo-services/',label:'Product and catalogue SEO'}]},
  {id:'b2b-engagement',eyebrow:'Scope and Reporting',title:'Agree What Success',highlight:'Can Be Measured Against',body:['We begin with the priority services, target market, existing pages and available evidence. The resulting plan identifies page owners, content requirements, technical dependencies and the first implementation sequence. The proposal states responsibilities and review points rather than promise a fixed ranking result.','Reporting separates visibility and clicks from enquiries, demos or opportunities recorded in a reliable system. We do not label traffic as pipeline when that connection is missing. Country and page-level views help distinguish growth in useful discovery from a wider but less relevant query mix.','Share the website, the work you want to win and examples you can publish. We will assess the fit before recommending a broader content programme.']}
 ],
 faqs:[
  {question:'Is B2B SEO the same as SaaS SEO?',answer:'No. SaaS campaigns often involve product features, integrations, comparison pages and trials or demos. This page focuses on consultancy and professional-service evaluation. We use our separate SaaS scope when the product journey calls for it.'},
  {question:'Do you guarantee qualified leads?',answer:'No. Search visibility is only one part of acquisition. We work on relevant pages and enquiry paths, but lead quality also depends on the offer, market, qualification and sales process. Commercial outcomes are reported only where they can be measured reliably.'},
  {question:'Do we need separate pages for every industry?',answer:'Only where the service, buyer questions and credible evidence are different enough to justify them. We review existing ownership first. An unsupported list of sector pages can create duplication without helping a buyer assess fit.'},
  {question:'Can you work with our internal subject experts?',answer:'Yes. Your team supplies the technical and commercial knowledge needed to keep service claims accurate. We agree review responsibilities and approval points before reader-facing content or implementation is released.'},
  {question:'Can the campaign cover more than one country?',answer:'It can, where you have a viable offer and the resources to support those markets. We separate country research and measurement, and use international SEO planning when regional architecture or country-page ownership needs work.'}
 ]
};
---
<FocusedServicePage data={data} />
